Generated by: Claude Code CLI
Date time: 2026/09/07 02:55 SAST
Version: 0.6
Description:
  The public tag index: every active label in the catalogue, sized by how much of it each one holds.

  It is not the same thing as the rail on a browse page, which offers a couple of dozen tags as a way
  to narrow what is already on screen. This is a way to find out what the catalogue is about before
  narrowing anything, which is why both exist.

  Sizing is five steps rather than a continuous scale, computed in the controller. A cloud sized by
  raw proportion becomes unreadable the moment one tag runs away with the catalogue, and nobody can
  tell one point of type size from the next in any case. The count is printed beside every tag, so
  the size is a hint and never the only information.

  A tag holding nothing is listed rather than hidden, and reads as empty. A reader here is being
  shown what the vocabulary is, and a term nobody has used yet is exactly the thing worth seeing.

  Comments here are plain prose only: no angle brackets, no comment delimiters, no template tokens
  and no code. Each of those is read as markup rather than as text.

Changelog:
  2026/09/07 02:55 SAST
  - Created for the v0.6 public tag index.
